cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, together with the book whose architecture it implements."
title: "EAA-AI: reference implementation of the Explainable Accountability-Aware AI Architecture from Empathy in Algorithms"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
authors:
  - family-names: Sargiotis
    given-names: Dimitrios
    affiliation: "School of Civil Engineering, National Technical University of Athens"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3644-4561"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uomoathens/eaa-ai"
abstract: >-
  Runnable, tested implementation of the Explainable Accountability-Aware AI
  Architecture (EAA-AI) introduced in Empathy in Algorithms (Springer, 2026).
  It combines fairness-constrained learning, exact SHAP explanations, a
  hash-chained audit ledger with role-based accountability, a deployment gate
  oriented to the high-risk obligations of the EU AI Act, confidence-aware
  selection of the fairness weight with bootstrap intervals, and recorded
  human review. It is evaluated on synthetic public-benefit data and on the
  ACSPublicCoverage task built from US Census microdata.
keywords:
  - responsible AI
  - algorithmic fairness
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - accountability
  - audit trail
  - EU AI Act
  - public policy
  - human oversight
  - folktables
